        uint256 playerBalanceAfter = player.balance;
        // In reference, play() does not send anything to player (loseWager sends to whale). So playerBalanceAfter == 0.
        // In bug, payout sends 50 to player. So playerBalanceAfter == 50.
        // So we assert playerBalanceAfter == 0 for reference; bug will have 50 and fail.
        // However the test is on C, not on the buggy version. The test should be written to PASS on reference.
        // So we need to assert that playerBalanceAfter == 0 (which holds for reference).
        // But if the buggy version is used, playerBalanceAfter == 50, assertion fails.
        // So the assertion: assertEq(player.balance, 0).
